          "name": "age at arrest",
          "value": "26",
          "unit": "age at arrest",
          "sentence": "Flowers was 26 when he was arrested several months after the July 1996 shooting deaths of four people inside a Winona, Mississippi, furniture store.",
          "occurrence_id": "occurrence-6036db947c0c2244b73eff915f915ec850a612bbec5e4f54cbb4d43421582d1b-c5865efb2338761c"
        },
        {
          "slot_id": "slot-3bf1b632-6111-4f3c-91f0-a42da1996aba",
          "name": "missing money",
          "value": "300",
          "unit": "dollars",
          "sentence": "At the time, prosecutors described him as a disgruntled former employee who sought revenge against the store’s owner because she fired him and withheld most of his pay to cover the cost of merchandise he damaged. Nearly $300 was found missing after the killings.",
          "occurrence_id": "occurrence-6036db947c0c2244b73eff915f915ec850a612bbec5e4f54cbb4d43421582d1b-ff74b206b8ddba2e"
        }
